  <Placemark>
   <name>Flood Advisory issued October 10 at 2:02PM EDT until October 10 at 5:00PM EDT by NWS Jacksonville FL</name>
   <styleUrl>#sev_minor</styleUrl>
   <Style>
    <BalloonStyle />
   </Style>
   <Snippet>* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.

* WHERE...Southeastern Atkinson County in southeastern Georgia...
Northwestern Bacon County in southeastern Georgia...
Southeastern Coffee County in southeastern Georgia...
South Central Jeff Davis County in southeastern Georgia...
Northwestern Ware County in southeastern Georgia...

* WHEN...Until 500 PM EDT.

* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...
- At 202 PM EDT, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain due to
thunderstorms. Minor flooding is ongoing or expected to begin
shortly in the advisory area. Between 1 and 1.5 inches of rain
have fallen.
- Additional rainfall amounts of 1 to 2 inches are expected over
the area. This additional rain will result in minor flooding.
- Some locations that will experience flooding include...
Nicholls, Bickley, Millwood and Axson.
- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood</Snippet>
