   </Style>
   <Snippet>* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.

* WHERE...Southeastern Clarendon County in central South Carolina...

* WHEN...Until 215 PM EDT.

* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...
- At 120 PM EDT, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain due to
thunderstorms. Minor flooding is ongoing or expected to begin
shortly in the advisory area. Between 1 and 3 inches of rain have
fallen.
- Some locations that will experience flooding include...
Santee Cooper Regional Airport, Davis Station and Foreston.
- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood</Snippet>
