   <name>Flood Warning issued October 10 at 10:33AM EDT by NWS Jacksonville FL</name>
   <styleUrl>#sev_severe</styleUrl>
   <Style>
    <BalloonStyle />
   </Style>
   <Snippet>...The Flood Warning continues for the following rivers in Georgia...
Florida...

St Mary's River At Macclenny affecting Nassau, Charlton and Baker
Counties.

Additional information is available at
https://water.weather.gov/wfo/JAX

The next statement will be issued Sunday morning at 1045 AM EDT.

* WHAT...Minor flooding is occurring and minor flooding is forecast.

* WHERE...St Mary's River at Macclenny.

* WHEN...Until further notice.

* IMPACTS...At 12.0 feet, Minor flooding of low lying areas and
timber lands including some properties along St. Mary's River Bluff
Road and the Cypress Landing Resort on the Georgia side. At 14.0
feet, Flooding of bottomlands along the river and some lower access
roads including the lower half of St. Mary's River Bluff Road which
cuts off 15 to 20 homes on the Georgia side.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...
- At 9:45 AM EDT Saturday the stage was 12.3 feet.
- Forecast...The river is expected to rise to a crest of 12.7 feet
tomorrow morning.
- Flood stage is 12.0 feet.
- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood</Snippet>
